      "On the fateful evening of the 2nd of October, while playing whist with his customary partners at the Reform Club, the conversation turned to a celebrated bank robbery in London. 'The world has grown small,' remarked Phileas Fogg in his calm, unhurried voice. 'A man can travel round the world in eighty days.' 'In theory, perhaps,' retorted Andrew Stuart, 'but not in practice, with railway delays, storms at sea, and shipwrecks!'",
