      "'Good,' said Mr. Fogg. 'The train leaves for Dover at eight-forty-five this very evening. I will take it. I shall be back in this very room of the Reform Club on Saturday, the 21st of December, at eight-forty-five in the evening; in default of which the twenty thousand pounds now deposited in my name at Baring Brothers will belong to you.' And packing only a modest carpetbag, accompanied by his faithful French valet Passepartout, Phileas Fogg embarked on the greatest race against time the world had ever witnessed.",
