      "The Emperor of Lilliput, accompanied by his imperial court and thousands of guards, came to inspect the Man-Mountain, as they called me. He commanded his officers to make an exact inventory of everything found in my pockets. Two Lilliputian secretaries climbed into my pockets with pen and paper, producing a document of comical precision: 'In the right coat-pocket of the Great Man-Mountain, we found a piece of coarse cloth, large enough to serve for a carpet in your Majesty's state room; in the left pocket, a huge silver chest, containing a sort of dust which made us sneeze violently for an hour; in his fob pocket, a wonderful engine that made a incessant noise like that of a water-mill, which we conjecture to be either some unknown animal, or the god that he worships.'",
