      "When I waked it was broad day, the weather clear, and the storm abated. But that which surprised me most was, that the ship was lifted, by the swelling of the tide, off the sandbank where she lay, and was driven up within about a mile of the shore. I saw that if we had all kept on board, we had been safe; and as the ship still stood upright, I resolved, if possible, to get on board, that I might save some necessary things for my preservation.",
