      "On the sled, in a long narrow box, lay the body of a man whom the Wild had conquered. In front of the box, and behind the dogs, toiled two men—Bill and Henry. They were wrapped in furs and soft-tanned leathers. Eyelashes and cheeks and lips were so coated with the crystals from their frozen breath that their faces were not discernible. This gave them the seeming of ghostly masqueraders, undertakers in a spectral world at the funeral of some corpse.",
